{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>וְהִשִּׂיאוּ אוֹתָם</b> and so forth. The meaning: when they do not pay the principal and the fifth, they enlarge the fence of the guilt that they committed unwittingly, so that it is called intentional, which is an actual sin, since it is within their power to remedy it and they do not remedy it. And that is what the verse says <b>וְהִשִּׂיאוּ</b> — meaning, they will bear them, that is, they will cause the matter to be considered a sin for them, when it was only a guilt-offering. And the verse's saying <b>בְּאָכְלָם אֶת קָדְשֵׁיהֶם</b> — meaning that the eating of the consecrated things that they ate will be reckoned to them as intentional, not as the mere inadvertence of withholding payment. And see what I explained in the preceding verse:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:00:19.416894710Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}